The board then proposes $\Phi^3$, $\Phi^4$, and $\Phi^n$ as exercises. There is a compact rule. For any ordinary function $W$, $\left.W(\Phi)\right|_{\bar\theta\theta}
=W'(\phi)D-W''(\phi)\bar\psi\psi.$ For $W(\phi)=\phi^2$, this reproduces Eq. [eq:l7-superfield-square]; for $W(\phi)=\phi^n$, it gives $\left.\Phi^n\right|_{\bar\theta\theta}
=n\phi^{n-1}D-n(n-1)\phi^{n-2}\bar\psi\psi.$  (Editorial clarification: The lecture assigns the $n$-th power as an exercise and states the expected kinds of terms. Equation [eq:l7-function-top-component] supplies the completed rule in the fixed ordering convention.)

